    <h2 class="broadsheet-title" style="font-size: clamp(1.7rem, 3.4vw, 2.5rem);">Things on the bench.</h2>

    <div class="broadsheet-body">
      <p>I keep a small workshop of half-built things. Most of them never become anything; a few become tools, fewer become essays, and the rest sit on the bench reminding me what I was thinking about three months ago.</p>

      <p>The honest version: a tool is a piece of judgment miniaturized into a form you can hand to someone else. Most of mine are still mine alone &mdash; not because they're secret, but because they aren't generous enough yet to deserve a stranger's attention.</p>

      <p>What appears here is the small set that has earned, or is close to earning, that generosity. The rest live in my local repo and in notebooks. If you want one of them and it isn't here, ask.</p>

      <p class="broadsheet-pull">"Build the tool the engagement asked for."</p>

      <p>I tend to build tools <em>during</em> consulting engagements rather than before them. A client problem reveals the shape of a missing instrument; I build the instrument; sometimes it survives the engagement. The ones that survive end up here.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="broadsheet-folio">
